  "details": "The only numeric operator missing aside from modulus which is in progress is the bitwise not operator which flips the bits on an integer type. The operator is also called the bitwise complement operator. In C# you'd use the ~ character to use this operator on an integer. It would be nice to have this for completeness.\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-reference/operators/bitwise-and-shift-operators#bitwise-complement-operator-",
